    "hoursNote": "The kitchen takes its last order 30 minutes before close.",
    "story": "<p>Copper Thistle opened in 2019 in a former ship chandlery on Harbor Street, with one wood-fired oven and a menu that changed every week.</p><p>Chef Maria Alvarez cooks with what the boats and farms around Portland bring in: day-boat scallops, oysters from the Damariscotta River, and vegetables from three farms within an hour of the kitchen. If it isn't in season, it isn't on the menu.</p><p>The room seats forty-two, with eight more at the bar. Come for a weeknight supper or a long Saturday lunch; either way, we'd like you to stay a while.</p>",
